window.EN={"1":"Thus the battle of Leif and his companions, which began in the village of Fiana, produced a result of sorts in the form of the liberation of northern Thracia.","2":"But the fighting was not yet over.","3":"In southern Thracia, the Kingdom of Thracia led by Travant holds great power,","4":"and in the Grannvale Empire, the Loptr Church and Prince Julius, called the incarnation of the dark god Loptous, still stand strong.","5":"Gran Year 777. The age was about to enter a new phase...","6":"Chapter 1: The Warrior of Fiana — cleared in ○○○ turns","7":"Chapter 2: The Coast of Ith — cleared in ○○○ turns","8":"Chapter 2x: Pirate Island — cleared in ○○○ turns","9":"Chapter 3: The Gate of Kelves — cleared in ○○○ turns","10":"Chapter 4: The Dungeon — cleared in ○○○ turns","11":"Chapter 4x: The Hero of Wind — cleared in ○○○ turns","12":"Chapter 5: Mother and Daughter — cleared in ○○○ turns","13":"Chapter 6: Escape — cleared in ○○○ turns","14":"Chapter 7: The Shield of Thracia — cleared in ○○○ turns","15":"Chapter 8: Purple Dragon Mountain — cleared in ○○○ turns","16":"Chapter 8x: Dagdar's Mansion — cleared in ○○○ turns","17":"Chapter 9: The Crest of Nova — cleared in ○○○ turns","18":"Chapter 10: Noel Canyon — cleared in ○○○ turns","19":"Chapter 11: Fort Dandrum — cleared in ○○○ turns","20":"Chapter 11x: Murder Holes — cleared in ○○○ turns","21":"Chapter 12: The Thieves of Dakia — cleared in ○○○ turns","22":"Chapter 12x: Dandelion — cleared in ○○○ turns","23":"Chapter 13: The Fortress City — cleared in ○○○ turns","24":"Chapter 14: All-Out Attack — cleared in ○○○ turns","25":"Chapter 14x: In Search of Freedom — cleared in ○○○ turns","26":"Chapter 15: Two Roads — cleared in ○○○ turns","27":"Chapter 16: The Norden Line — cleared in ○○○ turns","28":"Chapter 17: Leonster Gate — cleared in ○○○ turns","29":"Chapter 16: The Dark Forest — cleared in ○○○ turns","30":"Chapter 17: May Rain — cleared in ○○○ turns","31":"Chapter 18: Liberation of the Capital — cleared in ○○○ turns","32":"Chapter 19: The Empire Strikes Back — cleared in ○○○ turns","33":"Chapter 20: The Prince of Light — cleared in ○○○ turns","34":"Chapter 21: The War of Liberation — cleared in ○○○ turns","35":"Chapter 21x: The Prison Camp — cleared in ○○○ turns","36":"Chapter 22: The River Crossing — cleared in ○○○ turns","37":"Chapter 23: The Demon King's Castle — cleared in ○○○ turns","38":"Chapter 24: The Baron in Black — cleared in ○○○ turns","39":"Chapter 24x: The Altar of Loptous — cleared in ○○○ turns","40":"Final Chapter: The Sword of Oaths — cleared in ○○○ turns","41":"~ Overall Record ~","42":"Total: cleared in ○○○ turns","43":"Survivors: ×× people","44":"Overall rank: SSS SS S AAA AA A B C D E","45":"Game Design ■ Scenario Shouzou Kaga (already in English in the game)","46":"Super Advisor Kentarou Nishimura (already in English in the game)","47":"Program Chief Tohru Narihiro (already in English in the game)","48":"System Program Takafumi Kaneko (already in English in the game)","49":"Cp Program Chikara Yamamoto (already in English in the game)","50":"Effect Program Takanori Hino (already in English in the game)","51":"Event Program Ryuichirou Kouguchi (already in English in the game)","52":"Graphic Chief Masahiro Higuchi (already in English in the game)","53":"Character Graphic Sachiko Wada Yuka Hongou (already in English in the game)","54":"Battle Animation Ryou Hirata Maki Takemori (already in English in the game)","55":"Map Design Junko Umehara (already in English in the game)","56":"Character Design Mayumi Hirota (already in English in the game)","57":"Scenario Masayuki Horikawa (already in English in the game)","58":"Sound Create Yuka Tsujiyoko (already in English in the game)","59":"Sound Create ■ Sound Program Atsuko Matsumoto (already in English in the game)","60":"Sound Support Kenichi Nishimaki (already in English in the game)","61":"Art Work Taeko Kaneda Fujiko Nomura Yasuo Inoue (already in English in the game)","62":"Publicity Yuusuke Kitanishi (already in English in the game)","63":"Special Thanks Masatoshi Okuno Takaya Fujii Super Mario Club (already in English in the game)","64":"Producer Takehiro Izushi (already in English in the game)","65":"Leif, Prince of Leonster","66":"Together with Prince Seliph, he led the war to liberate Jugdral. Even after the victory at Belhalla he fought on from place to place,","67":"and his fame is said to have surpassed even that of the Holy King Seliph.","68":"In Gran Year 780, he founded the \"New Kingdom of Thracia,\" uniting north and south Thracia, and took its throne.","69":"Together with his queen Nanna and his sister Altena, he loved the people of Thracia above all,","70":"and as \"the one who carries on the will\" of Dain and Nova, he went on devoting his life to the unity and prosperity of his homeland.","71":"The name of the wise King Leif will never be forgotten, for as long as Thracia has a history...","72":"Together with Prince Seliph, he led the war to liberate Jugdral. Even after the victory at Belhalla he fought on from place to place,","73":"and his fame is said to have surpassed even that of the Holy King Seliph.","74":"In Gran Year 780, he founded the \"New Kingdom of Thracia,\" uniting north and south Thracia, and took its throne.","75":"Together with his sister Altena, he loved the people of Thracia above all,","76":"and as \"the one who carries on the will\" of Dain and Nova, he went on devoting his life to the unity and prosperity of his homeland.","77":"The name of the wise King Leif will never be forgotten, for as long as Thracia has a history...","78":"Finn, the legendary lance knight","79":"After seeing Leif's coronation through, he suddenly vanished from people's sight.","80":"It was three years later that he appeared again.","81":"Where he went and what he did in those \"three blank years\" is not recorded at all in the official histories.","82":"There remains only a stray account that someone saw him in the Yied Desert.","83":"Nanna, Princess of Nordion","84":"After the victory at Belhalla, she threw herself into the war to liberate Agustria together with Prince Leif.","85":"Later she was wed to Leif, King of Thracia, and devoted all her strength to the relief of orphans.","86":"For her loveliness and kindness, even after she became queen, the people","87":"fondly called her \"Princess Nanna,\" and it is told that her life was a happy one.","88":"Eyvel, the goddess of Fiana","89":"She returned to Fiana and for a while passed a peaceful time.","90":"With the disappearance of the \"geis,\" the pact with the dragon tribe,","91":"she regained her memory seven years after the victory in the holy war.","92":"The tale of her reunion with her children will surely be told again someday, to the sound of a bard's lute...","93":"Mareeta, swordswoman of the moon and stars","94":"Ashamed of her own immaturity in having been controlled by a cursed sword, she set out alone on a journey of training.","95":"In time she too grew into a swordswoman whose name was known across the whole continent,","96":"but all her life, it is said, she kept saying, \"I am nowhere near my mother.\"","97":"Dagdar, former bandit of Purple Dragon Mountain","98":"He returned to Purple Dragon Mountain, gathered his former men together, and began once more to take on the cultivation of the wasteland.","99":"After several years, the area around Purple Dragon Mountain is said to have been reborn as rich land.","100":"Tanya, the daughter Dagdar loved","101":"She moved to Fiana, later married, and was blessed with many children.","102":"With her forthright nature and a helpfulness bordering on meddling,","103":"she was relied upon and held dear by the villagers all her life, it is said.","104":"Halvan, the quiet hero","105":"After Eyvel was gone, he became the leader of Fiana village.","106":"He showed his talent as a lord as well, and Fiana village grew into a village so prosperous that its neighbors envied it.","107":"Osian, the raging axe fighter","108":"He returned to Fiana, later married, and was blessed with many children.","109":"His open-handedness and quick temper never changed his whole life,","110":"and as \"the village's famous old man\" he was, it is said, a presence people kept at arm's length yet relied upon.","111":"Marty, the man Dagdar loved","112":"He returned to Purple Dragon Mountain and, with his former comrades, began once more to take on the cultivation of the wasteland.","113":"A little slow, but with his simple, unaffected character, he was well loved by his comrades' children, it is said.","114":"Ronan, youth of Ith village","115":"He went home to Ith, where his mother waited, and returned once more to the life of a hunter.","116":"Later he married and seems to have led a modest but happy life.","117":"Safy, one who serves God","118":"She returned to Tahra and devoted her strength to saving the sick and the poor.","119":"It is told that the sight of her appeared to people's eyes just like that of a goddess.","120":"Tina, the playful sister","121":"Even after returning to Tahra she drifted about as ever, and kept those around her on edge, it is said.","122":"Did the day ever come when she settled down?","123":"Unfortunately, no history book has records that go that far.","124":"Lifis, the shy thief","125":"For a while he held an official post, but eventually he disappeared from it.","126":"Around the same time, the pirates' islands were completely subdued by the Kelves garrison.","127":"No record remains of anyone having seen him after that.","128":"Fergus, the carefree free knight","129":"After the war, he left like the wind.","130":"A prince of the blood of Connacht's royal house, or the hidden child of the legendary knight Beowolf,","131":"he was a man about whom rumors never ceased, but by now there is no longer any way to know.","132":"Karin, the girl who rides a pegasus","133":"She returned to her home, Silesse, and joined the \"Pegasus Knights\" she had longed for.","134":"After that, no notable achievements remain on record,","135":"but she seems to have become an excellent pegasus knight.","136":"Misha, one of Silesse's four pegasus knights","137":"She returned to Silesse and was welcomed into the \"Pegasus Knights.\"","138":"In the Silesse liberation war that followed, her distinguished service was remarkable, and she became the first commander of the pegasus knights of the reborn Kingdom of Silesse.","139":"As an able and fair commander, she was trusted deeply by those above and below her alike, it is said.","140":"Ced, crusader of the wind","141":"He returned to Silesse and, giving way to the people's ardent wishes, took the throne.","142":"Through his indomitable spirit and tireless effort,","143":"Silesse, laid waste by war, slowly but steadily comes back to life as the beautiful land it once was.","144":"Asbel, the boy guided by the wind","145":"In the liberation war he walked the road of hardship to the very end at Leif's side as his close aide.","146":"After the war he returned to Frest, the place of his birth, and succeeded his father as a priest.","147":"It would be a dozen or more years later still that the name of the sage Asbel became known in every corner of the continent.","148":"Brighton, knight of Munster","149":"He returned to Munster and poured his strength into rebuilding it, while teaching people the sword on the side.","150":"Later, it is said, he opened a small shop with his wife.","151":"Machyua, swordswoman of the gale","152":"She returned to Munster and poured her passion into rebuilding it.","153":"In time she married a former comrade-in-arms and bore a child,","154":"but her passion for rebuilding Munster never changed all her life, it is said.","155":"Lara, the lovely thief","156":"She went back to her original trade of \"dancer\" and kept dancing all over Thracia.","157":"Her beautiful \"dance,\" brimming with life, in time became a symbol of Thracia's revival,","158":"and gave courage to many people, it is said.","159":"Dalsin, a man of fiery passion","160":"Volunteering himself, he took up a post at Fort Kelves, and fought bravely day and night against thieves to protect people's livelihoods.","161":"As a result, the gangs of thieves around the fort were all but destroyed.","162":"In time, the \"place more fearsome than hell\"","163":"came to be praised as the \"place safer than heaven,\" it is said.","164":"Hicks, the axe knight with a child","165":"Taking no official post, he returned to his home village and led a peaceful life with his family.","166":"But even while working, he kept an axe planted at his side,","167":"and it is said he never neglected to be prepared for an emergency.","168":"Shiva, mercenary of Savan","169":"After the war ended, he slipped away without anyone knowing.","170":"About him there are far too many mysteries,","171":"and various theories have been put forward about his origins and what came after, but not one is certain.","172":"Glade, the dutiful lance knight","173":"He was appointed \"Grand General,\" the highest military rank among the retainers, and entrusted with reorganizing the overgrown army.","174":"He succeeded in making the army small and elite by reassigning surplus personnel and introducing new troop types,","175":"and greatly helped the kingdom as it suffered from financial difficulty, it is said.","176":"Selphina, the beautiful bow knight","177":"After New Thracia was founded, she resigned as commander of the royal guard, took children who had lost their parents into her mansion, and became a mother to them.","178":"The small lives Selphina saved in time bloomed greatly and produced many heroes who would carry the next age.","179":"Hence the knight Selphina was also called the Mother of Thracia, and her strength and kindness were spoken of into later ages, it is said.","180":"Cain, lance knight of Leonster","181":"He laid down his sword and became a civil official.","182":"In reorganizing the army, in policies for restoring the land and more, he carried out bold measures one after another,","183":"and as a \"taciturn man of practical affairs,\" he was deeply trusted by Leif and successive prime ministers, it is told.","184":"Alva, lance knight of Leonster","185":"He took up a post in the old Thracia region and, under the King's sister Altena, worked to restore public order.","186":"At first he seems to have been shunned by the people as \"a man of the north,\"","187":"but his natural cheerfulness and frank character won over the hearts of what were, at bottom, simple people, it is said.","188":"Robert, bow knight of Leonster","189":"At his own strong request, he was assigned to New Thracia's royal guard.","190":"He himself seems to have meant to be doing his best as a veteran knight,","191":"but his unreliability and haplessness were secretly the talk of the ladies-in-waiting at court, it is said.","192":"Carrion, the young noble of Leonster","193":"At Leif's wish, he took up a post at Meath Castle together with Hannibal.","194":"From then on he skillfully held together north and south Thracia, which were apt to strike discordant notes,","195":"and contributed greatly to the \"unification\" of north and south, it is said.","196":"Xavier, the loyal old general","197":"With Leif and the others, he devoted his strength to the founding of New Thracia.","198":"His opinions, backed by rich experience and knowledge, were always on the mark,","199":"and he was prized in the royal government of New Thracia's founding period, in which there were many young people, it is said.","200":"Fred, paladin of Friege","201":"After the war he returned to the Duchy of Friege and, aiding his young lord, devoted his strength to his homeland's revival.","202":"He was later wed to a young woman of his lord's line, but the difference in their ages was such that those around him teased him greatly, it is said.","203":"Olwen, the blue mage knight","204":"After the war she returned to the Duchy of Friege and, aiding her young lord, devoted her strength to her homeland's revival.","205":"When she thinks of her brother Reinhardt, she feels anger at how pitiable he was, the knight Olwen later said.","206":"Perhaps for that reason, the partner she chose was a man so ordinary that it surprised those around her, it is said.","207":"Perne, thief of Dakia","208":"Leaving the words \"I'm going back home,\" he left Leif and the others, after which all word of him ceased.","209":"As for him after that,","210":"there are various theories, such as \"it seems he went back to the thieving trade\" and \"he lent his strength to Tahra's revival.\"","211":"Troude, the man called the Reaper","212":"In the confusion right after the war's end, he vanished from people's sight.","213":"What became of him afterward is not certain,","214":"but according to various accounts, he seems to have gone back to a bodyguard's life.","215":"Salem, the dark mage","216":"After the war ended, he shut himself away in a remote countryside and set down his own experiences in a memoir.","217":"The memoir of Salem, who had once been a member of the Loptr Church,","218":"would come to be prized as a valuable historical source that observed from within just what Loptr had been.","219":"Linoan, the flower that blooms in Tahra","220":"She returned to Tahra and restored this city ravaged by war.","221":"She achieved a prosperity greater than before, and helped Leif's great work from behind the scenes.","222":"But despite her beauty, she remained unmarried all her life,","223":"which would invite all manner of speculation from later generations.","224":"Dean, the hero of the blue skies","225":"After the war ended, he protected the wounded Arion and returned to old Thracia.","226":"It would be several years later that he appears again on the main stage of history,","227":"as head of the dragon knights of the reborn Thracian army.","228":"Eda, dragon knight of Thracia","229":"After New Thracia was founded, as a close aide to Altena, she kept encouraging her while she was sunk in despair.","230":"Because of her earnest nature, she never sought her own happiness,","231":"and devoted her life to the revival of her homeland Thracia and to loyalty to Altena, it is said.","232":"Homer, the wandering bard","233":"As a bard he traveled all over Thracia and kept singing the saga of Leif and his companions.","234":"That saga, based on his own experience, was loved by the people of Thracia more widely than any other saga, it is said.","235":"Ralf, the drifter mercenary","236":"He exchanged his sword for farm tools and poured his strength into the revival of devastated Thracia.","237":"About Ralf afterward, nothing at all is handed down beyond this.","238":"Did Ralf choose to become one of the countless people who support the foundations of recovery, and be buried in history...?","239":"Ilios, the ambitious knight","240":"In the New Kingdom of Thracia, he at last became the noble he had longed to be.","241":"But he seems not to have been suited to peacetime administration, and failed in managing the region entrusted to him.","242":"As a \"meritorious retainer of the founding,\" he was not severely punished,","243":"but he was shunted to a sinecure of honor only, and would catch hold of his subordinates and repeat tales of his old exploits in arms, it is said.","244":"Sleuf, priest of Bragi","245":"Even after the war ended he did not return to the Tower of Bragi, but wandered the continent spreading the teachings of Edda.","246":"Through the earnest missionary work of the Edda priests, beginning with this Sleuf,","247":"the Edda Church came once more to gather faith as the spiritual support of many people.","248":"Amalda, the troubled lady knight","249":"She returned to Friege and devoted her strength to the revival of the Duchy of Friege.","250":"Friege's national strength had been exhausted by the destruction of the main Friege house in northern Thracia,","251":"but through the earnest efforts of Amalda and the others, it gradually regained the brilliance of former years.","252":"Shannam, the tall-tale swordsman","253":"Without serving New Thracia, he returned to his home, Isaach.","254":"After that, it is told, he quit the mercenary work that didn't suit him and led a respectable life.","255":"Miranda, the willful princess","256":"While waiting for Leif in Ulster, she fell in love with a certain knight and simply disappeared, it is said.","257":"Because of her fierce temperament she was often misunderstood, but it is told that she led a happy life as a wife and as a mother.","258":"Conomor, knight of Ulster","259":"He gave up knighthood and retired to private life.","260":"Thereafter he made his home on the outskirts of Ulster and quietly lived out his remaining years, it is said.","261":"Diarmuid, the knight of charisma","262":"After the war ended, he headed for Agustria together with his cousin, Prince Ares.","263":"Through their efforts, the unified Agustria would achieve unprecedented development.","264":"Galzus, the black swordsman of Od","265":"After Munster's liberation, he vanished to parts unknown.","266":"About him thereafter, even counting the official histories, the various accounts, stray reports and sagas, no record remains at all.","267":"Did he vanish into the darkness of history, or was he buried in the darkness of history? There is no way to confirm even that.","268":"Saias, priest of the red flame","269":"He returned to Velthomer and devoted his strength to rebuilding that land.","270":"At the request of the Holy King Seliph, who saw promise in his talent, he served the reborn Kingdom of Grannvale and contributed greatly to rebuilding the kingdom.","271":"Sara, the girl of sorrowful fate","272":"She quietly disappeared.","273":"According to various accounts, under Leif's protection she led a modest but rich-hearted life.","274":"In Chapter ○○, ×××× (chapter title): missing","275":"In Chapter ○○, ×××× (chapter title): died","276":"In Chapter ○○, ×××× (chapter title): felled by △△△","277":"In Chapter ○○, ×××× (chapter title): died of poison","278":"In Chapter ○○, ×××× (chapter title): self-destructed with the Devil Axe","279":"Fin"};
